Two different things live in this repository.

MIT (see LICENSE) — the tooling and the text written here:
  build.py, test_build.py, install.sh, SKILL.template.md, hooks/, .claude-plugin/,
  the hand-written parts of README.md, and the role files
  skills/agent-dispatcher/roles/{version-control,data-engineer,incident-responder}.md.

THIRD-PARTY, terms unknown — the other 24 role files and everything generated from them:
  skills/agent-dispatcher/roles/*.md (the other 24), skills/agent-dispatcher/SKILL.md,
  commands/agent-*.md, and the roles table in README.md.

Those 24 roles come from the "Locus Agent Template Pack v1.0.0" (18 September 2026, 24
templates), a third-party content pack. The adaptation here replaced that pack's runtime,
mode, memory-scope, and access-level vocabulary with this harness's equivalents and dropped
its grading metadata — but the working methods, deliverables, boundaries, and mode guidance
are substantially verbatim from the pack, in places word for word. Treat this as
redistribution of that text, not as an independent rewrite.

The pack states no license: it contains no copyright line, no terms of use, and no
redistribution grant. There is therefore no recorded permission to redistribute this
derived text.

Before making this repository public, or redistributing it in any form, obtain and record
an explicit license or written permission from the pack's author. If that is not
obtainable, the 24 derived role files have to be rewritten from scratch or dropped, leaving
the three roles original to this repository.
